# Copy this file to `.dockerignore` in the event project (the asset has no leading dot so it
# is easy to see and to copy). It keeps secrets (.env files) and build noise out of the image.
# deploy.sh only WARNs when `.dockerignore` is missing or has no .env* rule; the build goes on.
#
# `**/` makes a pattern match at any depth (a plain `node_modules` only matches the root).
# Markdown files are NOT excluded: a project may serve or read them at runtime.
#
# Adapt to the stack: this keeps `dist` and `.next` OUT of the build context. A Vite or
# TypeScript project that builds on the laptop would ship an image without its build output,
# so it needs a build stage in its Dockerfile (npm run build inside Docker), the way the
# Next.js block of Dockerfile.node does.
.git
.next
dist
.venv
**/.env*
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
.hack
